      "observed": "The anodes of the Ethernet/PI status LEDs D24, D25, and D30 are tied together on net /NET0064, but that net contains only those three LED anode pins and is not connected to any supply rail or current source. The CM4 LED outputs are connected to the LED cathode side through resistors.",
      "expected": "For LEDs whose cathodes are driven by active-low/open-collector status outputs, the LED anodes should be connected to a supply rail such as +3V3 (or to a sourcing driver). Standard LED drive topology requires a complete current path from supply through the LED and current-limiting resistor to the sink.",
