        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3V3\") ... no nodes for D24, D25, or D30 ...)"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"89\") (name \"NET0075\") (node (ref \"Module2\") (pin \"17\") (pinfunction \"Ethernet_nLED2(3.3v)\") ...)) (node (ref \"R19\") (pin \"2\") ...))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"164\") (name \"Net-(D24-K)\") (node (ref \"D24\") (pin \"1\") ...)) (node (ref \"R19\") (pin \"1\") ...))"}
      ],
      "impact": "D24, D25, and D30 cannot light because their anode net is floating; Ethernet link/activity and Raspberry Pi activity status LEDs will not operate as intended.",
      "confidence": 0.74
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows a clear connectivity anomaly: the Ethernet/PI status LED anodes D24, D25, and D30 are left on a floating net with no supply connection, so those LEDs cannot illuminate. Other observed discrepancies appear to be reference-number shifts or documented open issues rather than functional deviations."
}

